    s = re.sub(r"— as a finished model of the SHAPE and level only, not to translate — the matching file of the Spanish pilot in `/home/claude/tools/target/es/` \([^)]*\)\.",
               "`/home/claude/tools/target/esdo/fix_briefs_esdo.py` is NOT for you. The base course `/home/claude/tools/target/es/` is the model of shape and level: read only the ONE file of it that matches your own (for a new file: `decks-a.js` + `extra-a.js` for decks, or the first lesson of `lessons-3.js` for lessons, with offset/limit). The profile `/home/claude/docs/profiles/en-esdo.md` is large: read §1, §2, §4, §7, §8, §9 and §10; skip §6.2 to §6.4, §11, §13, §14 and Sources.", s)
    i = s.index('YOU OWN:'); j = s.index('PRON:')
